  "exact_bilingual_statement": "# 00000001554\n\n**English.** Definition: Euclidean Ramsey properties mean that every two-coloring of the plane contains a monochromatic copy of a specified configuration. Conjecture: Every red-blue coloring of the plane contains a monochromatic unit equilateral triangle; and the unit version follows from Gallai's similarity images plus rational-affine combinatorial closure. (unit triangle Euclidean Ramsey)\n\n**中文。** 定义：欧氏 Ramsey 性质指任何二染色平面含单色指定构型。猜想：平面任何红蓝染色恒含单色单位等边三角形；且单位版本由 Gallai 相似像加有理仿射组合封闭。（单位三角形欧氏 Ramsey）\n",
  "source_scope_notes": "English and Chinese agree: every red-blue coloring of the whole Euclidean plane is claimed to contain a monochromatic unit equilateral triangle. The first clause fixes unit side length, so a scaled/similar monochromatic triangle is insufficient. No continuity, measurability or periodicity restriction on colorings is imposed. Refuting this precise universal first clause suffices without formalizing the vague asserted derivation from Gallai similarity images and rational-affine closure. Mathematical and Lean correctness remain separate reviews.",
